WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.113 --> 00:00:16.856
"I suppose your stepfather, Mr.

2
00:00:16.876 --> 00:00:20.777
Windibank, was very annoyed that you went to the ball," Sherlock Holmes said to our client.

3
00:00:20.797 --> 00:00:24.918
"No, he was actually very good about it," said Mary Sutherland.

4
00:00:24.938 --> 00:00:28.159
"As I remember, he just laughed and shrugged his shoulders.

5
00:00:29.079 --> 00:00:32.440
He said there was no use in denying anything to a woman because she would always get her

6
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:36.193
way. "So what happened after you met Hosmer Angel at the Plumbers' Ball?"

7
00:00:36.553 --> 00:00:36.933
I asked.

8
00:00:36.953 --> 00:00:38.634
"The next day Mr.

9
00:00:38.694 --> 00:00:40.175
Angel came to call on my mother and me.

10
00:00:41.055 --> 00:00:44.136
My stepfather was still in France on business," said Miss Sutherland.

11
00:00:44.156 --> 00:00:45.617
"I met Mr.

12
00:00:45.677 --> 00:00:46.717
Angel twice for walks.

13
00:00:47.598 --> 00:00:49.879
But after that my stepfather returned, so Mr.

14
00:00:49.939 --> 00:00:51.479
Angel couldn't come to the house anymore."

15
00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:53.000
This puzzled me.

16
00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:54.921
"Why couldn't he visit you?"

17
00:00:55.341 --> 00:00:55.721
I asked.

18
00:00:55.741 --> 00:01:00.363
"Well, my stepfather didn't like me to have visitors," said Miss Sutherland.

19
00:01:00.383 --> 00:01:03.304
"He said a woman should be happy with her own family.

20
00:01:04.152 --> 00:01:06.794
But I used to say to Mother that I didn't have my own family yet!"

21
00:01:06.814 --> 00:01:08.075
"Did Mr.

22
00:01:08.176 --> 00:01:09.437
Angel make an attempt to see you?"

23
00:01:09.817 --> 00:01:10.337
asked Holmes.

24
00:01:11.338 --> 00:01:12.339
"No, but he wrote to me."

25
00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:16.222
At that point Miss Sutherland's stepfather was going back to France in a week.

26
00:01:17.103 --> 00:01:20.866
Mr. Angel wrote and said it would be safer not to see her until her stepfather had gone.

27
00:01:21.787 --> 00:01:24.589
In the meantime he suggested that they write to each other every day.

28
00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:29.454
Miss Sutherland was the first person in her family to see the mail each morning, so she didn't

29
00:01:29.534 --> 00:01:30.114
fear that Mr.

30
00:01:30.134 --> 00:01:31.215
Windibank would find Mr.

31
00:01:31.255 --> 00:01:31.876
Angel's letters.

32
00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.473
"Were you engaged to the gentleman at the time?"

33
00:01:34.854 --> 00:01:35.374
asked Holmes.

34
00:01:35.394 --> 00:01:37.335
"Oh yes.

35
00:01:38.136 --> 00:01:40.077
We were engaged after the first walk that we took.

36
00:01:40.898 --> 00:01:45.681
Mr. Angel was a cashier in an office on Leadenhall Street and—" "What office?"

37
00:01:46.062 --> 00:01:46.762
Holmes interrupted.

38
00:01:46.782 --> 00:01:48.683
"That's the worst of it, Mr.

39
00:01:48.723 --> 00:01:50.265
Holmes," replied Miss Sutherland.

40
00:01:51.105 --> 00:01:51.646
"I don't know."

41
00:01:51.666 --> 00:01:53.427
"Then where did he live?"

42
00:01:53.807 --> 00:01:54.568
asked the detective.

43
00:01:54.588 --> 00:01:56.549
"He slept at the office."

44
00:01:56.569 --> 00:02:00.312
"Let me make sure I understand the situation," said Holmes.

45
00:02:01.292 --> 00:02:02.413
"You didn't know the name of Mr.

46
00:02:02.493 --> 00:02:04.353
Angel's office or its exact address.

47
00:02:05.234 --> 00:02:06.854
So how did you address letters to him?"

48
00:02:06.874 --> 00:02:11.536
"I sent them to the Leadenhall Street post office to be left there until he called for them."

49
00:02:12.417 --> 00:02:14.017
Miss Sutherland went on to say that Mr.

50
00:02:14.097 --> 00:02:15.318
Angel thought it was better that way.

51
00:02:16.218 --> 00:02:19.740
He didn't want the other clerks in his office to tease him about getting letters from a lady.

52
00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:24.642
Miss Sutherland offered to type her letters, so no one would see her feminine handwriting.

53
00:02:25.522 --> 00:02:25.922
But Mr.

54
00:02:25.962 --> 00:02:29.804
Angel didn't like the idea of her using a typewriter, even though he typed all his letters to

55
00:02:29.844 --> 00:02:34.646
her. "He said that when I wrote the letters, they seemed to come directly from me," said Miss

56
00:02:34.666 --> 00:02:38.989
Sutherland. "But when they were typed, he always felt that the machine had come between us.

57
00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:42.991
That just shows you how fond he was of me and the little things that he would think

58
00:02:43.092 --> 00:02:46.414
of." "That is most revealing," said Holmes.

59
00:02:46.434 --> 00:02:50.776
"It has long been a belief of mine that the little things are always the most important.

60
00:02:51.677 --> 00:02:53.478
Can you remember any other little things about Mr.

61
00:02:53.518 --> 00:02:54.278
Hosmer Angel?"

62
00:02:54.298 --> 00:02:56.320
"He was a very shy man, Mr.

63
00:02:56.360 --> 00:03:00.425
Holmes. He would rather walk with me in the evening than in the daylight because he hated to

64
00:03:00.445 --> 00:03:02.485
be noticed by anyone," said Miss Sutherland.

65
00:03:02.505 --> 00:03:05.446
"He was very modest and kind.

66
00:03:06.367 --> 00:03:07.447
Even his voice was gentle."

67
00:03:08.347 --> 00:03:11.888
Mr. Angel had suffered from a severe sore throat and swollen glands as a youth.

68
00:03:12.868 --> 00:03:14.989
As a result he spoke in a hesitant whisper.

69
00:03:15.829 --> 00:03:18.270
He was always well dressed, very neat and plain.

70
00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:21.811
"But his eyes were weak just like mine," said Miss Sutherland.

71
00:03:22.651 --> 00:03:24.692
"He wore tinted glasses to protect them from the light."

72
00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:27.573
"What happened when your stepfather returned from France?"

73
00:03:27.993 --> 00:03:28.374
I asked.

74
00:03:28.394 --> 00:03:32.236
"Mr. Angel suggested that we should marry before my stepfather came back.

75
00:03:33.136 --> 00:03:36.898
Mr. Angel was dreadfully serious and made me swear on the Bible that I would always be true

76
00:03:36.938 --> 00:03:38.219
to him no matter what happened."

77
00:03:38.239 --> 00:03:40.640
"What did your mother think about all this?"

78
00:03:41.121 --> 00:03:41.661
asked Holmes.

79
00:03:41.681 --> 00:03:45.423
"Mother said he was quite right to make me swear my love on the Bible.

80
00:03:47.084 --> 00:03:49.965
She said it was a sign of his passion for me," said Miss Sutherland.

81
00:03:49.985 --> 00:03:54.368
"She approved of him right from the beginning and was even fonder of him than I was."

82
00:03:55.256 --> 00:03:55.656
When Mr.

83
00:03:55.716 --> 00:04:00.377
Angel talked about getting married within a week, Miss Sutherland began to worry about what her stepfather would

84
00:04:00.417 --> 00:04:02.118
think. Both Mr.

85
00:04:02.198 --> 00:04:04.479
Angel and her mother said not to be concerned about Mr.

86
00:04:04.499 --> 00:04:05.159
Windibank, though.

87
00:04:06.039 --> 00:04:08.720
It would be fine to tell him about the wedding after it took place.

88
00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:12.041
"I didn't quite like that," Miss Sutherland confessed.

89
00:04:12.061 --> 00:04:16.602
"It seemed odd to ask for my stepfather's permission to wed because he was only a few years

90
00:04:16.682 --> 00:04:17.222
older than I.

91
00:04:18.082 --> 00:04:20.683
But I also didn't want to keep any secrets from my stepfather."

92
00:04:21.563 --> 00:04:22.384
So she wrote to Mr.

93
00:04:22.424 --> 00:04:25.357
Windibank in Bordeaux, France, where his company had its office.

94
00:04:27.037 --> 00:04:29.698
However the letter was returned to her unopened on the morning of the wedding.

95
00:04:29.718 --> 00:04:32.199
"Then your stepfather didn't receive the letter?"

96
00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:33.060
asked Holmes.

97
00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:38.222
"Apparently he had already left for England just before it arrived in France," said Miss Sutherland.

98
00:04:38.242 --> 00:04:41.183
"The preparations went on for a quiet ceremony.

99
00:04:42.063 --> 00:04:43.184
On the morning of the wedding, Mr.

100
00:04:43.284 --> 00:04:44.885
Angel arrived at our house by cab."

101
00:04:45.725 --> 00:04:49.607
There was room for only two people in the cab, so he put Miss Sutherland and her mother

102
00:04:49.647 --> 00:04:50.287
into the vehicle.

103
00:04:51.067 --> 00:04:52.988
Then he stepped into another cab right behind them.

104
00:04:53.804 --> 00:04:55.845
"We got to the church first, and when Mr.

105
00:04:55.925 --> 00:04:59.326
Angel's cab arrived, we waited for him to step out," said Miss Sutherland.

106
00:04:59.346 --> 00:05:00.907
"But he never did.

107
00:05:01.627 --> 00:05:04.648
When the cabman climbed down and looked inside the cab, no one was there!

108
00:05:06.229 --> 00:05:08.350
The cabman could not imagine what had happened to Mr.

109
00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:11.631
Angel because he had seen my fiancé get into the cab with his own eyes.

110
00:05:12.552 --> 00:05:14.653
That was last Friday, and I have not heard from Mr.

111
00:05:14.733 --> 00:05:15.273
Angel since."

112
00:05:15.293 --> 00:05:19.074
"It seems to me that you have been shamefully treated," said Holmes.

113
00:05:19.094 --> 00:05:21.175
"Mr. Angel abandoned you."

114
00:05:21.195 --> 00:05:22.676
"Oh no, sir!

115
00:05:23.552 --> 00:05:25.533
Mr. Angel was too good and kind to abandon me."

116
00:05:26.494 --> 00:05:30.057
All that morning her fiancé had been urging her to promise that she'd be true to him no

117
00:05:30.077 --> 00:05:30.857
matter what happened.

118
00:05:31.858 --> 00:05:35.801
Even if something unforeseen should separate them, she was to remember that she was pledged to him.

119
00:05:36.701 --> 00:05:38.642
And that sooner or later he would return for her.

120
00:05:38.662 --> 00:05:42.645
"It seemed strange talk for a wedding morning," admitted Miss Sutherland.

121
00:05:42.665 --> 00:05:45.507
"But what happened afterward gave meaning to it."

122
00:05:45.527 --> 00:05:48.029
"So you think that Mr.

123
00:05:48.089 --> 00:05:49.630
Angel met with some catastrophe?"

124
00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:50.911
Holmes asked Miss Sutherland.

125
00:05:50.931 --> 00:05:52.212
"Yes, sir.

126
00:05:53.064 --> 00:05:53.765
I believe that Mr.

127
00:05:53.845 --> 00:05:56.867
Angel expected some danger, or else he wouldn't have talked like that.

128
00:05:57.708 --> 00:05:59.570
And then I think that what he feared actually happened."

129
00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:01.992
"How did your mother take his disappearance?"

130
00:06:02.392 --> 00:06:02.792
I asked.

131
00:06:03.713 --> 00:06:06.275
"She was angry and said I was never to speak of the matter again."

132
00:06:06.295 --> 00:06:09.538
"And your stepfather," I said, "did you tell him?"

133
00:06:09.558 --> 00:06:13.201
"Yes, and he agreed with me that something must have happened to Mr.

134
00:06:13.261 --> 00:06:14.643
Angel," Miss Sutherland said.

135
00:06:15.563 --> 00:06:17.145
She wiped her eyes with her handkerchief.

136
00:06:17.165 --> 00:06:20.648
"But my stepfather thought I would hear from my dear Hosmer again."
